NAME
    mouse - PS/2 mouse demo (Path C phase 3)

SYNOPSIS
    mouse [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Takes over the framebuffer, then in a 60 fps loop polls the
    kernel's PS/2 mouse driver via SYS_MOUSE_POLL (89) and redraws a
    crosshair cursor at the current absolute position. A HUD strip at
    the bottom shows x / y / button state in real time. Runs for
    SECONDS (default 8), then releases the framebuffer.

    Cursor color encodes button state:
      no buttons → white
      left  held → red
      right held → blue
      middle held → yellow

KERNEL DRIVER
    The PS/2 mouse is driven by kernel/mouse.c. Bytes arrive on the
    i8042 data port (0x60) interleaved with keyboard scancodes; the
    keyboard polling path inspects i8042 status bit 5 (AUX) before
    each read and routes mouse bytes to mouse_process_byte() instead
    of into the scancode decoder. Three-byte packets are reassembled
    and the running (x, y, buttons) state is clamped to the VBE
    framebuffer dimensions.

EXIT STATUS
    0   framebuffer was painted and released
    1   framebuffer unavailable or already owned by another task

